; Copy to `supabase.cfg` (same folder) and fill in. That file is gitignored.
;
; Both values below are PUBLIC by design — the anon key ships inside every
; Supabase client and is safe to embed in the game binary. What makes it safe is
; Row Level Security: the key alone grants nothing, and every policy checks
; auth.uid(). See supabase/schema.sql.
;
; The `service_role` key is the real secret. It must never appear in this file,
; in this repository, or in a chat window. It bypasses every policy.

[supabase]
url = "https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co"
anon_key = "PASTE-YOUR-ANON-PUBLIC-KEY"
